# producing the file the sidecar container runs as /sc/peer_server2_local.py:
#
#   cp peer_server2.py peer_server2_local.py
#   patch -p0 peer_server2_local.py < patches/peer-server2-local.patch     # or apply by hand, it is 5 hunks
#
# Hunk 1-4: box-local paths (hook dir, model dir, b12x dir, log dir) -> the container mounts /w, /model,
#           /b12x, /logs. Nothing numerical changes.
# Hunk 5 (the one that matters): acknowledge the completed sequence counter FIRST and do the bookkeeping
#           (stats, bucket-override read, stats-file write, progress print) afterwards. In the upstream order
#           the GB300 spins on words[1] while the sidecar writes a stats file every ~2 s, which showed up as
#           periodic multi-ms waits under load. Behaviour of the kernels is unchanged; the handshake order is.
#
